From 1a5b50d1d6ce4bc517378d244a106f1220c794ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 39/57] dns: the provider's DNS as the fallback of a server
 reached through the WAN

When a server reached through the WAN fails, the query goes to the DNS of the provider, taken from
netifd for each uplink, the fastest first; a failure counts once per event and only for names the
provider resolved; the state is forgotten on a network reset, the list read again at most once in 30
s.

Made of these commits of the earlier series (branch archive/r25-1.14-commits):
  92b29fcb5 dns: fall back to the provider's DNS when a server reached through the WAN fails
  f3bc6de57 dns: take the provider's DNS from netifd for the output device, ask the fastest
  fe71d80d6 dns: test the decisions of the provider DNS fallback
  45bcdcef6 dns: count a failure of a server once per event, and only for names the provider resolved
  a9ead7078 dns: forget the state of the provider fallback of every server on a network reset
  82a4db1f8 dns: read the provider's servers again after a miss at most once in 30 s
  949fc49c0 dns: take the first query to a server off the goroutine that reads client queries
  1814af0f1 dns: use slices.Equal and slices.Contains for the provider's servers
  60bb116f8 dns: every message of the provider DNS fallback is a warning
  69ccd4a80 dns: the fallback asks the provider of every uplink through it; a list for each box

Pdk-Feature: dns-provider
Pdk-Zone: core
Pdk-Layer: 04
